# qmldir — explicit module manifest for quickshell/modules/lock/ (quick
# task 260827-833, LOCK-01). Mirrors every sibling module manifest's own
# standing instruction (see modules/osd/qmldir, modules/qmldir): any .qml
# type added to this directory that is NOT declared below becomes
# unresolvable to `shell.qml`'s `import "modules/lock"` — qml-import-check
# enforces this. Any FUTURE type added to this directory MUST do the same,
# in the same commit that creates it.
#
# Lock is NOT a singleton — shell.qml mounts one ordinary, always-on
# instance at shell root (the screencopy pre-warm has to run at shell
# start; see Lock.qml's own header). LockContinuity/LockCaelestia/
# LockRail/LockSplit/LockFocus are the five operator-approved layouts,
# selected by LockSurface.qml's own `layoutKey` switch — every one must be
# declared here the same commit it gains a `case` arm in that switch, or
# the arm references an unresolvable type.
module qs.modules.lock
Lock 1.0 Lock.qml
LockPam 1.0 LockPam.qml
LockSurface 1.0 LockSurface.qml
LockClock 1.0 LockClock.qml
LockField 1.0 LockField.qml
LockStatus 1.0 LockStatus.qml
LockContinuity 1.0 LockContinuity.qml
LockCaelestia 1.0 LockCaelestia.qml
LockRail 1.0 LockRail.qml
